      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The safety of calcium channel antagonists has become a controversial issue among cardiologists. Thus, the role of calcium antagonists in the treatment of myocardial infarction is reviewed, and the differences among the 3 classes of calcium channel antagonists, phenylalkylamines, dihydropyridines, and benzothiazepines, are discussed."},
